+// Relocation completeness for lite translations (ANAL-381 step P1a). Every absolute operand a
+// lite translation embeds must be recorded, so it can be given another process's addresses.
+// Two independent checks, over fixtures that between them hit every kind of operand:
+//   - a pointer scan: no 8-byte window (or 4-byte window, below 4 GiB) of installed code may hold
+//     an address in a sensitive range (the translator image, entry trampolines, translation tables,
+//     helper resources, the guest module, installed code, counters) outside a recorded operand;
+//   - a differential: a translation re-linked into another environment must equal that
+//     environment's own translation byte for byte. In-process, the guest base, table slots,
+//     counters and install address differ (one base above 4 GiB, one below). In a second process,
+//     the translator image, heap resources and the main table differ too.
+// Each omitted record kind must make both checks fail. A RelocAbsToDisp32 displacement is
+// relative, so only the differential can see one missing.
+
